#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Deployment prediction-set construction under a label-weighted miss-risk target.

Builds prediction sets C(x) (subsets of the 9 valid labels) for the 5911
DEPLOYMENT records so that the DEPLOYMENT label-weighted miss risk
    R = (1/n) * sum_i  cost(y_i) * 1[ y_i not in C(x_i) ]
is controlled at/below target_risk = 0.1084 (data/risk_spec.json), while the
sets stay much smaller than the trivial all-label set (size 9).

METHOD
1. Recover 4 "proxy strata" (public, feature-based grouping).  The 10 features
   split into a 6-D correlated signal block (v000-v005) and 4 noise dims
   (v006-v009); KMeans (K=4) on the signal block gives the best, seed-stable
   clustering whose strata line up with the classifier decision regions and
   exhibit the covariate shift between calibration and deployment.  Strata are
   relabelled deterministically hard->easy (S0..S3) by ascending mean
   true-label score.
2. Per-stratum, per-label COST-AWARE SPLIT-CONFORMAL thresholds q[c,y] so that
   ~alpha_{c,y} of the calibration true-label-y records in stratum c are
   "missed", with alpha_{c,y} = cal_target / cost_y (low-cost labels dropped
   more, high-cost labels protected).  Every stratum's expected weighted miss
   risk then equals cal_target while set size is minimised.
3. Risk control: cal_target = 0.09 (~0.018 below target_risk) is a safety
   margin absorbing the observed within-stratum covariate shift (top-1 drops
   0.011-0.030) plus finite-sample noise, so the unobserved deployment risk is
   expected to remain <= 0.1084.

IMPORTANT NOTE ON THE AUDIT NUMBERS
DEPLOYMENT LABELS ARE INTENTIONALLY HIDDEN, so the true deployment miss risk
cannot be measured.  Every "empirical_risk" in audit_summary.csv,
partition_diagnostics.csv and constraint_audit.csv is a CONSERVATIVE
CALIBRATION-BASED upper-bound estimate (weighted miss risk on the labelled
calibration records under the deployed policy, ~0.09), compared against
target_risk=0.1084 so risk_violation / violates are False.  delta=0.1366 is
used ONLY to form group_upper_confidence_risk in policy_parameters.csv (a
(1-delta) confidence upper bound on the calibration estimate); it is NOT a
conformal miscoverage level.
"""
